# FEATURE — PLAYER (Audio + Lyrics + Chords)

CRITICAL — CORE RUNTIME COMPONENT

This document describes the Player system.
It is the central component used during live performance.

All changes must preserve stability, timing accuracy, and user control.

⸻

USER GOAL

The user must be able to:
- play a song instantly
- see synchronized lyrics or chords
- control playback easily during live
- prepare the next track without stress
- maintain a smooth and professional flow

⸻

CORE RESPONSIBILITIES

The Player is responsible for:

- Audio playback (ExoPlayer)
- Timing reference (single source of truth)
- Lyrics / Chords synchronization
- Timeline event dispatch (MIDI / DMX)
- Playback transitions (next, auto-play, crossfade)
- Track-specific settings (gain, pitch, speed)

👉 The Player drives everything during live.

⸻

ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW

Main components:

- ExoPlayer (Media3)
- PlayerScreen (UI)
- MainActivity (state + player bridge)
- Timeline dispatcher (MIDI / DMX)
- Track settings stores (volume, pitch, tempo)

⸻

PLAYBACK MODEL

- Playback MUST use ExoPlayer only
- currentPosition is the global time reference

👉 All systems depend on this:
- lyrics
- chords
- MIDI
- DMX

No alternative timing system allowed.

⸻

PLAYBACK FLOW

1. User selects a track
2. Player loads the corresponding songId data
3. Audio source is resolved (local file)
4. Player prepares ExoPlayer
5. Playback starts

During playback:
- currentPosition is continuously read
- UI is updated
- timeline events are dispatched

⸻

PLAYER OPENING BEHAVIOR

The Player opening behavior is user-configurable.

Modes:
- Always:
  - Player opens every time a track is launched
- Never:
  - Playback starts but current screen remains visible
- Automatic:
  - Player opens only when the launched track has lyrics/chords or requires player display

Rules:
- Must not affect audio launch
- Must not delay playback
- Must not break lyrics loading
- “Always” must remain the safest fallback mode

Known risk:
- Automatic mode depends on reliable lyrics/chords detection.
- If detection is uncertain, prefer preserving lyrics display and playback stability.

⸻

LYRICS & CHORDS

- Lyrics and chords are independent layers
- Both are time-based (.lrc)

- UI can switch instantly between:
  - Lyrics mode
  - Chords mode

👉 No reload required

---

## LYRICS READABILITY MODE

The Player includes a readability display mode for lyrics.

Purpose:
- improve readability in bright daylight / outdoor live conditions
- allow the user to anticipate upcoming lyrics
- avoid depending only on the active highlighted line

Behavior:
- OFF:
  - active lyric line is fully visible
  - inactive lines use reduced opacity
- ON:
  - all lyric lines are displayed at full opacity
  - active line remains identifiable with highlight color, bold weight, and slightly larger size

Rules:
- must not affect lyrics timing
- must not affect scroll synchronization
- must not affect audio playback
- must be persistent across app sessions

UI:
- controlled from the top-left Player header icon
- toggle must be immediate and reliable

⸻

LYRIC LINE COLORS

Lyrics lines may have optional display colors.

Purpose:
- provide visual markers during live performance
- help identify important phrases, spoken parts, warnings, or structure changes

Behavior:
- color can be set from the lyric sync editor
- default/no color must remain supported
- colored lines must remain readable in Player
- color must persist after saving and reopening the song

Rules:
- Must not break standard LRC import/export
- Must not inject non-standard color tags into LRC text unless explicitly supported
- Color metadata must remain separate from timing text when possible
- No color must be treated as default behavior

⸻

LYRIC SYNC SELECTION UX

In the lyric sync editor:
- long press on an unselected line selects it
- long press on an already selected line deselects it

Rules:
- tap behavior must remain unchanged
- edit/delete/color dialog must remain available
- selection must not affect audio playback or timing

⸻

TIMELINE INTEGRATION

The Player drives timeline execution:

- MIDI cues
- DMX cues
- Notes / markers

Rules:
- based on time (ms)
- no dependency on UI
- deterministic triggering

👉 The Player is the clock.

⸻

TRACK SETTINGS (CRITICAL)

Each track can have:

- gain (volume adjustment)
- pitch
- speed
- trim IN / OUT

Rules:
- stored per songId
- applied at playback
- never modify original audio

👉 Settings must be stable and persistent.

⸻

TRANSITIONS

Supported behaviors:

- Play → immediate start
- Define Next → next track queued
- Auto Play → automatic chaining
- Crossfade → smooth transition
- Live transition fade → current track fades out while next track starts immediately

Rules:
- transitions must be predictable
- no glitch allowed
- no timing drift
- next track must become immediately active for UI/timeline
- old track must never continue driving lyrics/timeline after handoff

⸻

LIVE PLAYLIST HANDOFF (CRITICAL)

The Player must correctly receive and display playlist chaining information.

Rules:
- nextTrack must always resolve to a readable title
- Player must never display null next titles
- autoplay and live chain must survive UI recomposition
- playlist UI state must never be used as playback truth
- playback transitions must preserve nextTrack integrity
- live chaining must work independently from viewport/UI rendering

The Player must remain synchronized with:
- playlist order
- explicit Define Next
- live red group chaining

👉 Live continuity has priority over UI optimizations.

⸻

LIVE LIST / TEMPORARY QUEUE

The Player can interact with a temporary “Liste live”.

Purpose:
- allow the user to create a short live sequence while a track is already playing
- keep the next track visible and predictable
- chain selected tracks without stress

Expected behavior:
- if track A is playing and user creates a live list with track B:
  - A remains the current playing track
  - B becomes the next effective track
  - B must be visible as the next track in Player
  - B must start automatically at the end of A

Rules:
- Must not override a manually defined next track
- Must not interfere with DJ mode
- Must not create hidden or ghost nextTrack state
- Must remain deterministic after adding C, D, etc.

⸻

PRE-END BEHAVIOR (RETURN -10s)

- When enabled:
  - The Player automatically returns to the playlist view
  - approximately 10 seconds before the end of the current track

Purpose:
- Allow the user to anticipate the next track
- Prepare transitions without stress
- Maintain full control during live

Rules:
- Must NOT interrupt playback
- Must NOT affect audio timing
- Must NOT trigger any playback change

👉 This is a UI/navigation behavior ONLY
👉 Playback continues normally in background

Constraints:
- Timing must be based on ExoPlayer position
- Must be consistent across devices
- Must not trigger multiple times

Optional:
- Feature must be user-configurable (on/off)

⸻

DEFINE NEXT (LIVE CRITICAL)

- User can select the next track during playback
- The selected track must be clearly visible (UI feedback)
- It must start automatically at the end of the current track

👉 No ambiguity allowed

⸻

AUTO PLAY

- When enabled:
  - tracks follow playlist order automatically

- Must work with:
  - groups
  - reordered tracks

👉 Always deterministic behavior

⸻

SEEK BEHAVIOR

- Seek is allowed ONLY for navigation

FORBIDDEN:
- using seek for loops
- using seek for arrangement logic

👉 Seek must remain safe and predictable

⸻

## SEARCH EXIT AFTER TRACK LAUNCH

When a track is launched from search results, the search UI must close immediately.

Purpose:
- avoid returning to stale search results during live
- ensure the playlist/library is visible when the user comes back
- keep the -10s return workflow usable

Behavior:
- user searches for a track
- user launches a track from search results
- playback starts normally
- search closes immediately
- normal playlist/library view is restored

Rules:
- must not affect playback
- must not affect Define Next behavior
- must not clear unrelated playlist state
- search must remain reusable afterward

⸻

UI REQUIREMENTS

- Must be readable in live conditions
- Large text (lyrics / chords)
- Clear visual hierarchy
- readability mode for outdoor/daylight situations

Must provide:
- Play / Pause
- Next / Previous
- Define Next feedback
- Mode switch (Lyrics / Chords)

👉 No visual overload

⸻

PERFORMANCE RULES

- UI updates must be lightweight
- No heavy recomposition during playback
- No blocking operations

👉 Player must remain fluid at all times

⸻

STATE MANAGEMENT

- Player state must be explicit:
  - playing
  - paused
  - stopped
  - loading

- No hidden transitions
- No ambiguous states

👉 Predictable behavior only

⸻

ERROR HANDLING

- Playback must not crash
- In case of issue:
  - fail gracefully
  - keep UI responsive

👉 Never break the live experience

⸻

KNOWN PITFALLS

- Desync if timing not based on ExoPlayer
- Glitches if audio pipeline is unstable
- UI lag affecting perception of sync
- Misaligned trims causing bad transitions
- nextTrack lost during recomposition
- “Prochain : null” display
- playlist UI state incorrectly used as playback state
- crossfade keeping old timeline active
- autoplay breaking after reorder/group changes

👉 Must be tested carefully

⸻

TEST SCENARIOS (MANDATORY)

Test at least:

- play a single track
- switch Lyrics ↔ Chords during playback
- toggle lyrics readability mode during playback
- define next track during playback
- auto play sequence
- crossfade transitions
- live transition fade between tracks
- verify next title display during transition
- verify nextTrack survives reorder/group changes
- seek forward / backward
- track with trim IN / OUT
- track with pitch / speed
- return -10s behavior (enabled / disabled)
- launch a track from search and verify search closes
- Opening mode Always / Never / Automatic
- Automatic opening with lyrics track
- Automatic opening with no-lyrics track
- Create live list while A is already playing, verify B becomes next
- Add C and D to live list, verify chaining order
- Color a lyric line, save, reopen, verify persistence
- Long press selected lyric line again, verify deselection

👉 Must be tested on real device

⸻

FINAL RULE

The Player must ALWAYS feel:
- instant
- stable
- predictable

If a change introduces:
- delay
- confusion
- instability

👉 It must be rejected.